<div class="card">
    <h2>About this scenario</h2>
    <p>
        The system boundary is the checkout/counter queueing process only: a customer joins
        the queue once they reach the counter (Service Start Time in the report's terms is
        recorded here as Arrival Time into the queue), waits until the cashier is free, is
        served, and leaves. Browsing, fitting rooms, warehouse/inventory, online orders and
        delivery are explicitly out of scope. The men's and women's counters were observed
        as two separate queues and are never combined into a single queue in the
        single-server models below.
    </p>
</div>
